															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1922529&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605884059" alt="Agent MacLeod" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1922529)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;" >Agent MacLeod</a></span> <span class="odate time_1408062381 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Aug 2014 00:26</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2089114">
									

<p>To the best of my knowledge, there is no such thing as &quot;Level 3 Hazardous Materials suit.&quot; I just went over this on another SCP. I know that not everyone can be expected to know this stuff, but I don't think someone should be allowed to use technobabble based on real-life things if they don't know the real-life things. The UN standards for HAZMAT gear are as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li>Class A: Full body, pressurized protection. You won't come into contact with Hazardous Material unless something breaks the suit, which is unlikely.</li>
<li>Class B: Full body, unpressurized protection. You won't breathe the stuff in, and it probably won't touch your skin, but it's not an all-out spacesuit like Class A protective gear.</li>
<li>Class C: Full coverage, but unsealed. Air is provided by, to put it in layman's terms, a gas mask, and you won't be expected to deal with highly infectious or irritating materials.</li>
<li>Class D: Work clothes. You might as well be naked. You end up in a scenario that requires Class A protection in Class D protection, well, I'm sure someone will say something nice at your funeral.</li>
</ul>
<p>/rant<br />
As stated in the title, this a a nitpick. If you DGAF, I'll find a way to live with myself, somehow.</p>

							</div>

								
					
